WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.000
In an emergency, responders change faster than the situation.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.500
What gets lost is the consequence of what was already tried.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.000
Incident INC-2026-0817 - smoke near Machine 7. Critical.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Pressure rising on the Machine 8 header. Main power still live.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.500
Every observation is a durable row in CockroachDB.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.500
The obvious move: restart Machine 7 to clear the fault.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.800
Sentinel searches CockroachDB's vector index.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.500
Closest match: INC-2025-0412.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.900
The same restart. Pressure hit Machine 8.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.500
Sentinel recommends the safer sequence: isolate first.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.500
It cites the exact memories it used.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.500
A human approves. Sentinel never touches the machine.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.500
Decision, state and audit commit in one transaction.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Now the part that usually breaks everything.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
The backup starts with zero context.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.200
Except the incident was never stored in the agent.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Every step is auditable, end to end.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.200
Reconstructed from durable memory events in CockroachDB.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.000
The same retrieval is searchable directly.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.300
Similarity scores, latency, index used.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The backup rebuilds its briefing from the database.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.200
What happened, what was attempted, what must not be repeated.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.500
CockroachDB is the system of record. Bedrock reasons over it.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.800
Normal agents remember conversations.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.000
Sentinel remembers consequences.
